# ae2_feed

CC: Tweaked script for TerraFirmaGreg. **Only job:** discover storages + machines on a wired modem network, push **exactly N** of the current storage item into each free machine, evenly and as fast as CC allows (`sleep(0)` yield only).

## Not in scope

- No pattern providers / AE2 return path
- No draining machines
- No greenhouse / craft UI code

## Layout

Storages (crate/barrel/…) and identical GT machines on one wired network. Something else (AE2, pipes) fills storages; this script only splits into machines.

## Modules

- `config.lua` — `N`, optional explicit `STORAGES` / `MACHINES`, optional substr filters
- `discover.lua` — classify inventories (auto keywords or explicit lists)
- `move.lua` — count / free / distribute via `shared/transfer.lua`
- `main.lua` — hotplug rescan + feed loop

## Deploy

```text
python tools/bundle_project.py ae2_feed
```

Copy `dist/ae2_feed.lua` to the computer. Edit `N` in the bundled config section or in `ae2_feed/config.lua` before rebuild.

## Conventions

- Keep `require("transfer")` short names; bundler resolves `shared/`
- Prefer inventory-agnostic peripheral names from discovery/config — never hard-code a single crate/machine id in logic
- Free machine = zero count of the current input item (ready for a fresh N-set)
- Do not add timed sleeps; only `sleep(0)` for CC yield
